  "hypothesis": {
    "id": "prequential_crossfit_bounded_residual_calibration_of_sealed_incumbent",
    "claim": "A deterministic, strongly regularized residual calibrator trained only on chronologically earlier sealed Gen1 OOF cases can correct stable station/lead incumbent bias enough to reduce full-prefix integrated RMSE by at least 0.030 m, while a fixed inner evidence gate and exact identity fallback prevent unsupported corrections.",
    "structural_distinction": "The Gen6 candidate is the sealed incumbent plus at most 0.12 m of prequentially cross-fitted calibration. It does not replace, refit, blend, route, or retune the incumbent model and it never uses a current outer fold target to decide whether that fold is corrected.",
    "falsifier": "The hypothesis fails if the unchanged five-point meaningful-curve gate fails, if any inner gate fails and the corresponding output is not byte-exact to the incumbent, or if any central-ledger, leakage, reproducibility, candidate, test, or upload prohibition is violated."
  },
